## 2026-09-18

### Optional APPS module: local dev servers as systemd user services (#36)

**Augie Bralley** · GitHub [@auggernaut](https://github.com/auggernaut) · X [@augman](https://x.com/augman) · www.auggernaut.com

Registers a checkout with the start command it already has and a fixed port,
installs it as a systemd **user** service, and puts readiness, checkout, branch,
changed-file count, logs and Open/Start/Stop/Restart/Edit on the desk. Ships an
`infomarchy-apps` CLI so any terminal or agent gets the same `ensure` operation:
reuse the running service, or start it and wait for HTTP readiness.

The problem it solves: a dev server started in a terminal outlives that terminal,
the next task cannot find it, so it starts a second one on another port. Handing
the process to systemd means the desk only asks for actions and reads status, so
hiding the desk or closing an agent task cannot stop an app.

First thing in the plugin that writes outside its own config (unit files in
`~/.config/systemd/user`, a symlink in `~/.local/bin`), which is why the refusals
matter: it will not replace a unit lacking its own `# Managed by Infomarchy Apps`
marker, will not replace a `~/.local/bin` entry that is not its own symlink, and
reports a busy port with the owning PID and directory rather than killing,
adopting, or silently swapping it. Ownership is proven through the service cgroup
rather than inferred from the port. The module starts **disabled** and is the one
entry in the module strip needing an explicit `true`.

Merged f96507e. 329 tests pass on the merged tree. Scope accepted by Fred.

Note on the handle: Augie's GitHub declares `augustinbralley` in both the profile
field and social_accounts, but his own site says **@augman** twice. @augman is
correct, confirmed by Fred, who knows him in person.

